 # BossStreaks
-BossStreaks OSRS plugin+
+BossStreaks is a RuneLite external plugin that watches normal in-game boss kill-count chat messages and keeps a lightweight daily streak for each boss you kill.
+
+When a kill-count message such as `Your Zulrah kill count is: 150` appears, the plugin records that boss for the current local day. The first tracked kill on a new consecutive day extends the streak; a missed day resets that boss streak back to 1.
+
+## Features
+
+- Detects RuneLite game messages in the standard `Your <boss> kill count is: <count>` format.
+- Tracks streaks per boss for the current client session.
+- Avoids double-counting multiple kills of the same boss on the same day.
+- Posts a concise chat confirmation when a streak starts or advances.
+- Includes client-free unit tests for the parser and streak engine.
+
+## Configuration
+
+RuneLite config group: `bossstreaks`
+
+- `Show streak messages` (default: on): enables or disables BossStreaks chat notifications.
+
+## API usage
+
+BossStreaks does not call external APIs. It only uses RuneLite client chat events and local in-memory tracking, so there are no network credentials, rate limits, or third-party dependencies to configure.
+
+## Development setup
+
+This repository follows the standard RuneLite external plugin layout:
+
+- Main plugin: `src/main/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/bossstreaks/BossStreaksPlugin.java`
+- Config: `src/main/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/bossstreaks/BossStreaksConfig.java`
+- Streak engine: `src/main/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/bossstreaks/BossStreaksTracker.java`
+- Test launcher: `src/test/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/bossstreaks/BossStreaksPluginTest.java`
+- Unit tests: `src/test/java/com/itmeansbigmountain/bossstreaks/BossStreaksTrackerTest.java`
+
+Use Java 11 for local builds:
+
+```bash
+export JAVA_HOME=/opt/data/jdks/current-java11
+export PATH="$JAVA_HOME/bin:$PATH"
+```
+
+Run the automated checks:
+
+```bash
+./gradlew test --no-daemon -q
+./gradlew assemble --no-daemon -q
+```
+
+Launch RuneLite in developer mode for manual testing:
+
+```bash
+./gradlew run --no-daemon
+```
+
+## Manual testing checklist
+
+1. Start the plugin with `./gradlew run --no-daemon`.
+2. Confirm BossStreaks appears in the RuneLite plugin list and that `Show streak messages` is enabled.
+3. Kill a boss that emits a kill-count chat message.
+4. Confirm the chat box shows a message like `BossStreaks: Zulrah streak is now 1 day.`
+5. Confirm additional kills of the same boss on the same day do not increase the streak again.
+6. Test another boss to confirm streaks are tracked independently.
+
+## Plugin-hub prep notes
+
+Before plugin-hub submission, capture a screenshot or short GIF of the chat notification during a real RuneLite session and verify whether session-only streak tracking is acceptable or whether persistent streak storage should be added.
